{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"summary\":\"One concrete contract violation: null payloads are accepted despite the task requiring IllegalArgumentException.\",\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"F1\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"file\":\"src/main/java/com/toss/cashback/infrastructure/webhook/WebhookSignatureVerifier.java\",\"line\":58,\"description\":\"A null payload is converted to an empty string, so sign(secret, null) returns a signature and verify can authenticate it. Although the approved plan permits this, the task explicitly prohibits null payloads and requires IllegalArgumentException for invalid sign inputs.\",\"suggestedFix\":\"Validate payload alongside secret in both public methods and throw IllegalArgumentException when payload is null; remove the null-to-empty conversion.\"}]}"}}
